.TH PING 1
.SH NAME
ping \- send ICMP echo requests to a host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ping
.I host
.RB [ \-c
.IR count ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ping
finds the address of
.I host
(a name is resolved through DNS), sends an ICMP echo request one a second
(4 by default) and prints the time each reply took, or the error; then how
many were sent and how many came back. A reply that does not come within
2 seconds counts as lost.
.PP
.B ping
is another name of
.BR fetch (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " count"
Send
.I count
requests.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if at least one reply came back, 1 otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ping \-c 2 10.0.2.2
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR traceroute (1),
.BR host (1),
.BR fetch (1),
.BR netd (4)
